See JENKINS-75818.

In case custom plugins adds items to the breadcrumb the initial rendering is not collapsing the path but will as soon you resize the window. The solution proposed is to expose the computing of the collapse in a listener so custom plugins can trigger an event.
Testing done
On a custom plugin that does something like
(function () {
  var dataHolder = document.getElementById('extra-left-top-nav');

  var breadcrumbs = document.getElementById('breadcrumbs');
  var jenkinsRootBreadcrumb = breadcrumbs && breadcrumbs.firstChild;

  //Move the extra breadcrumbs into the breadcrumbs, at the left of the Jenkins Root Breadcrumb
  var extraBreadcrumbs = document.getElementById('extra-left-top-nav').childNodes;
  if (extraBreadcrumbs && extraBreadcrumbs.length) {
    var fragment = document.createDocumentFragment();
    while (extraBreadcrumbs && extraBreadcrumbs.length) {
      fragment.appendChild(extraBreadcrumbs[0]);
    }
    breadcrumbs.insertBefore(fragment, jenkinsRootBreadcrumb);
  }
  window.dispatchEvent(new Event("computeOverflow")) //this will fix the current problem not to collapse
})();


Proposed changelog entries

add window listener 'computeOverflow' to trigger a new compute of the breadcrumbs


