When a CredentialsParameterDefinition restricts "Credential type" to a specific type (e.g. "Secret text"), credentials returned by external providers as java.lang.reflect.Proxy instances (implementing only the public credential interfaces, as recommended in docs/implementation.adoc) were silently excluded from the dropdown, even though they correctly declare the official descriptor. Selecting "Any" worked because it bypassed type filtering entirely.
Root cause

decodeType() resolved the selected type to the concrete implementation class (e.g. StringCredentialsImpl) and used it both as the provider lookup type and the required match type.
Downstream providers filter with type::isInstance; a proxy implementing StringCredentials can never be instanceof StringCredentialsImpl, so it's dropped before it even reaches the UI layer.

Fix

CredentialsParameterDefinition.DescriptorImpl now always queries providers with the broad StandardCredentials.class (same as "Any"), so proxy-backed credentials aren't excluded at the provider level.
Type restriction is applied afterwards via a CredentialsMatcher that accepts a credential if it's either an instance of the concrete class or its getDescriptor() matches the descriptor for the selected type — the latter path covers proxy-backed credentials that correctly report the official descriptor.
decodeType replaced by decodeTypeDescriptor/decodeTypeMatcher; doFillDefaultValueItems/doFillValueItems switched from includeAs to includeMatchingAs with the new matcher.

private CredentialsMatcher decodeTypeMatcher(String credentialType) {
    CredentialsDescriptor descriptor = decodeTypeDescriptor(credentialType);
    if (descriptor == null) {
        return CredentialsMatchers.always();
    }
    return CredentialsMatchers.anyOf(
            CredentialsMatchers.instanceOf(descriptor.clazz),
            new DescriptorMatcher(descriptor) // matches credential.getDescriptor() == descriptor
    );
}
Tests

Added a test provider mimicking an external plugin's type::isInstance filtering, exposing a dynamic proxy for StandardUsernamePasswordCredentials delegating to a real UsernamePasswordCredentialsImpl, and asserting the proxy credential now appears when filtering doFillDefaultValueItems/doFillValueItems by the concrete type.



Fixes #1083

