Description
TeeBuildListener, TeeOutputStreamBuildListener, and TeeOutputStream compose a primary and secondary listener/stream so a build's console log is written to both places at once (used by OtelLogStorage to tee output to the OTel log sender and to the local FileLogStorage listener). Their close() methods closed the two delegates sequentially with no try/finally:
if (main instanceof Closeable) {
    ((Closeable) main).close();
}
if (secondary instanceof Closeable) {
    ((Closeable) secondary).close();
}
If the first close() throws (in OtelLogStorage, the primary is the OTel log sender, which can fail to close cleanly on a network/exporter error), the exception propagates immediately and the secondary delegate's close() is never called, leaking its underlying resource (e.g. the FileLogStorage file handle for that build). TeePrintStream in the same package already handles this correctly; this change applies the same "always attempt both, propagate the first failure with the second as a suppressed exception" pattern to the other three Tee* classes.
Fixes #1297
Testing done

Added TeeOutputStreamTest, TeeBuildListenerTest, TeeOutputStreamBuildListenerTest, each asserting the secondary delegate is closed even when the primary's close() throws.
