Moves the mapping from Key Vault secrets to Jenkins credentials behind a new extension point, AzureKeyVaultCredentialsAdapter, so other plugins can add their own credential types without changes here.
Also much simpler and safer handling of optional plugins here too.
Each adapter handles one value of the type tag and gets the secret's tags, ID, description, scope and a lazy lookup for the secret value (plus other secrets in the same vault).


The existing types (string, username, secretFile, sshUserPrivateKey, certificate, githubApp) are now adapters.


The GitHub App adapter uses @OptionalExtension, replacing the manual check for github-branch-source.


Added AzureKeyVaultCredentialsDescriptor so credential types are only offered by the Azure providers by default.


Fixed a NullPointerException for secretFile secrets without a fileName tag; it now falls back to <secret name>.txt as documented.


README has a short section on adding new types.


Add support for clientID for GitHub apps


Testing done
Used the below:

Script to generate secrets
VAULT=asdasdsadasdas

# string
az keyvault secret set --vault-name $VAULT --name test-string --value "hello-string"

# username / password
az keyvault secret set --vault-name $VAULT --name test-username \
  --tags type=username username=deploy --value "s3cret-password"

# secretFile, with and without a fileName tag (the second should come out as test-file-noname.txt)
az keyvault secret set --vault-name $VAULT --name test-file \
  --tags type=secretFile fileName=hello.txt --value "hello from key vault"
az keyvault secret set --vault-name $VAULT --name test-file-noname \
  --tags type=secretFile --value "no file name tag"

# SSH private key
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -N '' -q -f test-ssh
az keyvault secret set --vault-name $VAULT --name test-ssh \
  --tags type=sshUserPrivateKey username=deploy --file test-ssh

# certificate, with its password in a separate secret
openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -keyout test.key -out test.crt -subj "/CN=test" -days 30
openssl pkcs12 -export -inkey test.key -in test.crt -out test.p12 -passout pass:changeit
az keyvault secret set --vault-name $VAULT --name test-cert-password --value changeit
az keyvault secret set --vault-name $VAULT --name test-cert \
  --tags type=certificate password-id=test-cert-password --value "$(base64 -i test.p12)"

# GitHub App using the new clientID tag (dummy key, so it only checks the credential loads)
openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -pkeyopt rsa_keygen_bits:2048 -out test-gith
az keyvault secret set --vault-name $VAULT --name test-github-app \
  --tags type=githubApp clientID=Iv23liTest owner=my-org --file test-github


Pipeline
node {
  stage('string') {
    withCredentials([string(credentialsId: 'test-string', variable: 'STRING')]) {
      echo STRING.substring(0, STRING.length() - 2)
    }
  }
  stage('username') {
    withCredentials([usernamePassword(credentialsId: 'test-username', usernameVariable: 'USER', passwordVariable: 'PASS')]) {
      echo USER
      echo PASS.substring(0, PASS.length() - 2)
    }
  }
  stage('secretFile') {
    withCredentials([file(credentialsId: 'test-file', variable: 'FILE'), file(credentialsId: 'test-file-noname', variable: 'FILE2')]) {
      sh 'echo "file: $(basename "$FILE") ($(wc -c < "$FILE") bytes)"; echo "default name: $(basename "$FILE2")"'
    }
  }
  stage('sshUserPrivateKey') {
    withCredentials([sshUserPrivateKey(credentialsId: 'test-ssh', keyFileVariable: 'KEY', usernameVariable: 'SSH_USER')]) {
      sh 'echo "user: $SSH_USER"; head -1 "$KEY"'
    }
  }
  stage('certificate') {
    withCredentials([certificate(credentialsId: 'test-cert', keystoreVariable: 'KEYSTORE', passwordVariable: 'KS_PASS')]) {
      sh 'echo "keystore: $(wc -c < "$KEYSTORE") bytes"'
    }
  }
}

