Fixes #863
Fixes #1139
Fixes #1146
Two cases where Pipeline Overview showed a failed build without saying why.
Exceptions caught outside a stage (#863)
def var = null
try {
    node { stage('test') { echo 'test'; var.isEmpty() } }
} catch (err) {
    echo "Caught: ${err}"
}
test was marked failed, but the NullPointerException appeared nowhere. Exceptions were only found on the last node of the run, so once a try/catch swallowed the error, nothing was left to show.
Now every exception that escaped a block gets a Pipeline error step where it was thrown, whether or not something caught it further up. An exception passing through several blocks is shown once. AbortException and FlowInterruptedException are still left to the step that raised them, as before.
When the exception is thrown directly from a parallel branch, the step takes that branch's status and timing. A branch's end node shares the whole parallel block's relationship, so without this the error would show as running while a sibling branch was still going.
This also drops the Could not find BlockEndNode that threw exception SEVERE log (#1146), which was in the replaced code.
Failures outside every stage (#1139)
pipeline {
  agent { docker { image 'this-docker-image-doesnt-exists:latest' } }
  stages { stage('Test step') { steps { echo 'bla' } } }
  post { always { echo 'test' } }
}
Steps outside every stage were dropped as soon as the pipeline had any stage. The failed docker pull runs before the stages, so once post added the "Post Actions" stage, only "Post Actions" (success) was left.
Now, when a step outside all stages fails, is unstable or is aborted, the "System Generated" stage is kept to hold those steps. The stage is added after stages are remapped, so real stages are never nested under it. Its status is the combined status of the steps it holds (NodeRunStatus.combine), not the status of the whole run, so a caught failure outside the stages still shows as failed. The combined state is running, then paused, then queued, and finished only when every step is. Pipelines whose steps outside stages all succeed are unchanged.
PipelineGraphViewCache.SCHEMA_VERSION is bumped so builds that already finished get their graphs recomputed.
Testing done

Added seven tests to PipelineStepApiTest:

an exception caught outside the stage;
an uncaught exception after the stages;
an exception thrown from a parallel branch while a sibling branch is paused on a semaphore;
a failed step outside the stages next to another stage;
a caught failure outside the stages, checking the synthetic stage's own status;
a failed load body outside the stages;
a guard that successful steps outside stages add no synthetic stage.


Added NodeRunStatusTest for how statuses combine, including a queued step next to a finished failure.
The first three issue tests (caught exception, exception after the stages, failure next to another stage) fail on main. The three tests added for the review findings (parallel branch, synthetic stage status, load body) fail on this PR's first commit. All pass with both commits, and the guard passes throughout.
mvn clean verify passes on the rebased branch: frontend, plus 240 Java tests including the Playwright ones, with 0 failures and 1 skipped.
Ran both reporters' pipelines on Jenkins 2.589 with docker-workflow 653.v2f2c08eff0ec:

#863: test now contains Pipeline error with the NPE.
#1139: there is now a "System Generated" stage with the failed docker pull, next to "Post Actions".



