The GitHubFilterRefUtils.isBranchExcluded function fetches the commit for every branch before checking the name to see if it's the one to be filtered. This means during a full scan it will perform nested iteration over every branch, which scales quadratically could result in millions of lookups for a repository with >2000 branches.
This moves the getCommit call inside the name check, so each branch only has one lookup. The exclusion result is unchanged.
Event driven scans of a single branch were not affected, since getBranches() only returns that branch in that case.
Disclosure: I was evaluating this plugin with Claude and it flagged this issue and helped prepare and test the fix.
Testing done
I verified this locally with a throwaway test that mocks 2,000 branches (half older than the threshold), runs isBranchExcluded for each, and counts getCommit calls:

Before: 1,000 excluded, 2,001,000 commit lookups
After: 1,000 excluded, 2,000 commit lookups

The same branches are excluded either way.
mvn verify passes for all modules.

Test and output
class GitHubFilterRefUtilsTest {

    private static final int BRANCH_COUNT = 2000;
    private static final long NOW = System.currentTimeMillis();
    private static final long THRESHOLD = NOW - TimeUnit.DAYS.toMillis(30);

    private final AtomicInteger commitLookups = new AtomicInteger();
    private final List<GHBranch> branches = new ArrayList<>();
    private GitHubSCMSourceRequest request;

    @BeforeEach
    void setUp() throws IOException {
        GHRepository repo = stub(GHRepository.class);
        Map<String, GHCommit> commits = new HashMap<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < BRANCH_COUNT; i++) {
            String sha = String.format("%040d", i);
            long age = TimeUnit.DAYS.toMillis(i % 2 == 0 ? 365 : 1);
            GHCommit commit = stub(GHCommit.class);
            when(commit.getCommitDate()).thenReturn(new Date(NOW - age));
            commits.put(sha, commit);
            GHBranch branch = stub(GHBranch.class);
            when(branch.getName()).thenReturn(String.format("branch-%04d", i));
            when(branch.getSHA1()).thenReturn(sha);
            when(branch.getOwner()).thenReturn(repo);
            branches.add(branch);
        }
        when(repo.getCommit(anyString())).thenAnswer(invocation -> {
            commitLookups.incrementAndGet();
            return commits.get(invocation.<String>getArgument(0));
        });
        request = stub(GitHubSCMSourceRequest.class);
        when(request.getBranches()).thenReturn(branches);
    }

    private static <T> T stub(Class<T> type) {
        return mock(type, withSettings().stubOnly());
    }

    private boolean isExcluded(String branchName) throws IOException {
        return GitHubFilterRefUtils.isBranchExcluded(request, new BranchSCMHead(branchName), THRESHOLD);
    }

    @Test
    void excludesOnlyBranchesOlderThanThreshold() throws IOException {
        assertThat(isExcluded("branch-0000")).isTrue();
        assertThat(isExcluded("branch-0001")).isFalse();
        assertThat(isExcluded("does-not-exist")).isFalse();
    }

    @Test
    void fullScanLooksUpOneCommitPerBranch() throws IOException {
        int excluded = 0;
        for (GHBranch branch : branches) {
            if (isExcluded(branch.getName())) {
                excluded++;
            }
        }
        System.out.printf(
                "Full scan of %d branches: %d excluded, %d commit lookups%n",
                BRANCH_COUNT, excluded, commitLookups.get());
        assertThat(excluded).isEqualTo(BRANCH_COUNT / 2);
        assertThat(commitLookups.get()).isEqualTo(BRANCH_COUNT);
    }
}
