Fixes #14698
Problem
FileParameterValue's @DataBoundConstructor dereferences file.getName() with no null check:
@DataBoundConstructor
public FileParameterValue(String name, FileItem file) {
    this(name, file, FilenameUtils.getName(file.getName()));
}
Stapler's JSON-binding machinery invokes this constructor from FileParameterDefinition#createValue(StaplerRequest2, JSONObject), the code path used by the modern "Build with Parameters" form submission, with a null file whenever the submitted form has no file attached for that parameter (as originally reported on an iPad browser, but reproducible with any client that omits the multipart part for an empty file input). The resulting NullPointerException surfaces as an unhandled 500 error instead of a clean message.
The sibling method, FileParameterDefinition#createValue(StaplerRequest2) (the legacy/CLI path), already treats a missing upload as "no value" rather than an error:
if (src == null) {
    // the requested file parameter wasn't uploaded
    return null;
}
The JSON-binding path never got the same treatment.
Fix
Since the constructor itself has no way to signal "no value" back to its caller (unlike createValue, which can return null), reject the missing file with hudson.model.Failure, which Stapler already renders as a clean error page instead of a stack trace, matching the pattern used throughout this class elsewhere in core (e.g. PluginManager, ListView, ComputerSet).
Testing done
Added FileParameterValueTest#dataBoundConstructorRejectsMissingFileCleanly (core/src/test), which calls the constructor directly with a null file and asserts it throws Failure rather than NullPointerException. Confirmed the test fails with the exact reported NPE before the fix, and passes after. Ran the existing test/src/test FileParameterValueTest suite (15 tests, covering the SECURITY-1074/1424/3927 path-traversal regressions) with no regressions, plus checkstyle and spotless.
Proposed changelog entries

Fixed an unhandled 500 error when submitting a "Build with Parameters" form with no file attached for a file parameter.

